# What never needs to reach a build.
#
# deploy.sh does not actually use this file: it tars the context itself, with the same list spelled
# out as tar --exclude flags, because `gcloud builds submit` cannot stage source with the
# permissions this account has (see cloudbuild.yaml). This file exists so that anyone who *does*
# run a plain `gcloud builds submit .` gets the same context, and it is the third copy of the list
# alongside .dockerignore and deploy.sh. Keep the three in step.
#
# Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which would exclude nothing useful and include
# .git — several hundred megabytes of history for a build that only needs the checkout.
.git/
.gitignore
target/
out/
bench/
tests/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
